WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.336
-This is "Know Your Bro"
with J.J., Derek, and T.J. Watt.

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:06.673
Welcome, family. Welcome, guys.
Thank you for playing.

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:09.842
This is fun. Now, look,
you guys all play in the NFL.

00:00:09.842 --> 00:00:11.678
But more importantly,
you're brothers.

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:14.914
So I thought -- you're close,
but I want to see just how close

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:16.348
you are in a game
called "Know Your Bro."

00:00:16.348 --> 00:00:18.918
Here's how it works.
One of you will wear headphones

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:21.087
while the other two answer
a question about you,

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:23.256
then that brother
will take off the headphones

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:25.458
and say what he thinks
the answer is.

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:28.594
If the answers match,
you get a point. Make sense?

00:00:28.594 --> 00:00:30.129
-Sounds good.
-Sounds good.

00:00:30.129 --> 00:00:32.231
-All right. Cool.
Let's do this.

00:00:32.231 --> 00:00:35.000
T.J., the first question
is about you,

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.070
so please put on
your headphones.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.205
This question is about T.J.

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:41.641
And give us a thumbs up
when you cannot hear us.

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:44.510
Ready?
T.J. is the youngest.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:47.146
What is the biggest problem
that the older Watt brothers

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:50.950
ever had to help T.J.
get out of?

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.452
-Oh, I mean, that --

00:00:53.452 --> 00:00:56.222
that definitely has to be
when we were in Italy.

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:57.557
-Okay.

00:00:57.557 --> 00:00:58.557
-You know what
I'm talking about?

00:00:58.557 --> 00:00:59.792
-Yep. Yep. Oh. Easily.

00:00:59.792 --> 00:01:02.395
-Really? What was that?
What was that?

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:04.197
-So, we took a brothers' trip

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:05.865
one year
at the end of the season,

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:08.568
and we went all around Europe
for 14 days,

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.970
and Italy was one
of the last stops.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.338
And so we stopped in Italy,

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:16.442
and T.J.'s very, very allergic
to tree nuts, and so --

00:01:16.442 --> 00:01:19.144
But we didn't know
that pesto had tree nuts in it.

00:01:19.144 --> 00:01:20.513
None of us did.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:21.915
I mean, it's actually one of the
main ingredients of pesto,

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:23.416
we now know.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.551
So, we're in
an Italian restaurant,

00:01:25.551 --> 00:01:27.486
and T.J. orders pesto.

00:01:27.486 --> 00:01:30.322
And we're sitting down literally
right outside the Pantheon,

00:01:30.322 --> 00:01:31.891
and he's eating the pesto,

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:33.626
and all of a sudden
he literally cannot breathe,

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:35.861
and he's blowing up
like Will Smith in "Hitch."

00:01:35.861 --> 00:01:37.964
And so we're freaking out.

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:41.534
Derek and I, we take him, get
in a cab, go to the hospital.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.402
They take T.J. to the back.

00:01:43.402 --> 00:01:46.606
Derek and I are stuck in
the waiting room by ourselves.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.308
Can't see him.
Don't know where he is.

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:51.644
-I just remember,
where we were waiting,

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:54.346
there was a little TV screen
up there with, like --

00:01:54.346 --> 00:01:57.049
You had a number, but
we didn't know T.J.'s number.

00:01:57.049 --> 00:01:59.118
It was, like,
eight numbers long.

00:01:59.118 --> 00:02:01.688
And there was a green circle,
a red circle,

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:04.156
and a yellow circle
next to those numbers,

00:02:04.156 --> 00:02:06.459
and we have no clue
what number T.J. is.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:08.327
And there's all these
different-colored circles

00:02:08.327 --> 00:02:10.162
next to these numbers and --
-You're hoping he's green.

00:02:10.162 --> 00:02:11.463
-No clue how he's doing.

00:02:11.463 --> 00:02:12.932
-Yeah, just please
be green, man. Please.

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:15.135
-We have no clue how he's doing.
We're sketchy.

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:17.570
Everything was just --
It was insane.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.339
-Okay. All right. All right.
Good. That's crazy.

00:02:20.339 --> 00:02:22.141
I mean, it turned out okay,
obviously. All right.

00:02:22.141 --> 00:02:24.677
So -- T.J.?

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:27.179
All right, T.J.,
we heard this --

00:02:27.179 --> 00:02:30.416
Thank you for doing this.
I asked your brothers what --

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:32.251
Since you're the youngest one,
what's the biggest problem

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:35.688
that the older Watt brothers
ever had to help get you out of?

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:39.358
-The biggest problem they ever
had to help me get out of?

00:02:39.358 --> 00:02:40.893
-There's a lot.

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:42.562
-Oh, Italy.
-Yeah.

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:45.632
-Italy. Oh, yeah.
-That was scary, huh?

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:47.800
-We ate the pesto over in Italy,

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.936
and then we had to
rush over to the hospital.

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:53.306
And then we were in the back,
and J.J. and Derek said

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:55.308
they were looking at the screen
or whatever,

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:57.109
and people didn't know
what a tree nut was,

00:02:57.109 --> 00:02:59.212
and it was a whole thing.
It was bad.

00:02:59.212 --> 00:03:01.113
-That's right.
Ding, ding, ding, ding.

00:03:01.113 --> 00:03:02.415
Correct.

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:04.817
That's a match.
That's a match right there.

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:06.985
This question is for Derek.

00:03:06.985 --> 00:03:09.188
Derek, can you put on
the headphones, please?

00:03:09.188 --> 00:03:10.423
-Yep.

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:12.725
-This next question
is going be about you.

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:14.260
All right. Ready, guys?

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:17.096
I heard that Derek
was the best athlete

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:19.031
out of all the Watts growing up.

00:03:19.031 --> 00:03:22.101
When were the older brothers
the most jealous of Derek?

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:24.770
-Well, I played with Derek in
high school and then in college,

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:26.672
and then I'll play with him
this year in the NFL.

00:03:26.672 --> 00:03:28.641
In high school, Derek was

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:30.944
absolutely a beast
on the football field.

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:33.446
I mean, he was running back.

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:36.882
He played linebacker.
He kicked field goals.

00:03:36.882 --> 00:03:39.418
He punted. He returned kicks.

00:03:39.418 --> 00:03:41.387
By far the best high-school
football player

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:42.789
I've ever seen in my life.
By far.

00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:44.723
-I agree. I agree with that.

00:03:44.723 --> 00:03:46.425
And I will say this.
He was so good --

00:03:46.425 --> 00:03:49.195
This, still, I don't fully
understand it to this day.

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:50.863
Their homecoming week --

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:52.298
You know, every homecoming week
has a theme.

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:54.367
Like, it's James Bond
or it's A Night in Paris

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:55.635
or whatever it is.

00:03:55.635 --> 00:03:59.471
The homecoming theme for
Derek's year was Black and Watt,

00:03:59.471 --> 00:04:01.040
and they just
put pictures of him

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.276
all over the hallways
and all over the gym.

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:05.578
It was the most wild thing
I've ever seen.

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:09.114
-It's like he's Ferris Bueller?
-Yeah, it was unbelievable.

00:04:09.114 --> 00:04:11.751
I thought
it was a joke at first,

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:13.986
and then I, like, talked
to everybody at the school,

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:17.023
and they're like, "No,
he's the homecoming theme."

00:04:17.023 --> 00:04:19.225
And I still can't
wrap my head around it.

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:21.594
-Not the king or anything.
He's the theme.

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:23.329
-The theme.

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:26.399
-All right, all right.
Let me get him right now.

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:28.200
The question
I asked your brothers was,

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.902
when were they
most jealous of you?

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:33.239
What was the thing they'd be
most jealous of you for?

00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:35.608
-I had a hom--

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:38.544
This is J.J.'s favorite thing
he always talks about --

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:42.614
is homecoming my senior year,
everything was decorated.

00:04:42.614 --> 00:04:44.850
Like, there was a theme,
and it was Black and Watt.

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:47.686
Like, I was our
homecoming theme.

00:04:47.686 --> 00:04:50.990
I don't know --
I did not know it was happening.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:52.825
I walked to school,

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:55.094
and it was homecoming
Black and Watt.

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:57.129
My face was everywhere
and said --

00:04:57.129 --> 00:04:59.865
It actually even said
"Good-bye, J.J., hello, Derek"

00:04:59.865 --> 00:05:01.066
on the lockers.

00:05:01.066 --> 00:05:02.668
[ Laughter ]
-Wow!

00:05:02.668 --> 00:05:04.103
-And it just --
-We got it.

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:05.704
-We got it.
We get it. We get it.

00:05:05.704 --> 00:05:07.407
[ Laughter ]
-That's amazing.

00:05:07.407 --> 00:05:09.074
That's like
a Ferris Bueller story, dude.

00:05:09.074 --> 00:05:11.310
That's unbelievably cool.
-Ferris Bueller.

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:13.145
-All right. Our last one --
That was a match.

00:05:13.145 --> 00:05:15.047
Our last one here is for J.J.

00:05:15.047 --> 00:05:18.917
J.J., can you put some
headphones over your headphones?

00:05:18.917 --> 00:05:20.786
You're the first person
to wear two sets of headphones,

00:05:20.786 --> 00:05:23.422
by the way.
-I saw Tom Brady do it once.

00:05:23.422 --> 00:05:25.324
-Okay. Ready, guys?

00:05:25.324 --> 00:05:26.792
-Yep.
-Good.

00:05:26.792 --> 00:05:28.627
Being the oldest sibling

00:05:28.627 --> 00:05:30.329
means sometimes
you're the babysitter.

00:05:30.329 --> 00:05:34.266
When did J.J. fail the hardest
at babysitting?

00:05:34.266 --> 00:05:37.036
-Babysitting.

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:39.806
The chicken story, Derek.
-Chicken story for sure.

00:05:39.806 --> 00:05:41.607
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:43.242
-I love the name of it already.

00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:45.611
-So I'm pretty sure --
Yeah, we've got it named.

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:47.279
I'm pretty sure --
We were about --

00:05:47.279 --> 00:05:48.648
J.J. was, like, 12,

00:05:48.648 --> 00:05:51.083
so I was probably about 8,
and T.J. was 6.

00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:53.886
And we were all home alone.
J.J. was babysitting.

00:05:53.886 --> 00:05:55.988
And he was trying to, you know,

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:58.591
be the great older brother
and cook for all of us.

00:05:58.591 --> 00:06:03.095
And so he decides to grab
a glass tea kettle,

00:06:03.095 --> 00:06:05.764
put it on the burner,
directly on the burner,

00:06:05.764 --> 00:06:07.833
grab some chicken breasts
out of the fridge,

00:06:07.833 --> 00:06:10.302
and throw them
into the glass tea kettle.

00:06:10.302 --> 00:06:11.904
-No water.

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:13.739
-No water.
Just expects them to cook.

00:06:13.739 --> 00:06:16.608
He's never seen
our mother or father do this.

00:06:16.608 --> 00:06:18.677
Trying his own technique.

00:06:18.677 --> 00:06:21.113
I believe actually, too,

00:06:21.113 --> 00:06:24.717
he had gone to shower
while this was happening.

00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:27.120
So T.J. and I are
sitting out there.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:29.622
Clearly this is going wrong.

00:06:29.622 --> 00:06:32.191
Smoke coming out of
this tea kettle everywhere.

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:34.593
J.J. comes running out
in a towel.

00:06:34.593 --> 00:06:36.328
-Yeah, I think it was
a "save himself" thing.

00:06:36.328 --> 00:06:38.831
I don't even think he grabbed us
and brought us out of the house.

00:06:38.831 --> 00:06:40.866
-He didn't.
I think he saved himself.

00:06:40.866 --> 00:06:41.967
-Unbelievable.

00:06:41.967 --> 00:06:44.403
-We were scared.
And we didn't eat.

00:06:44.403 --> 00:06:46.538
-[ Laughs ]
Scared and hungry.

00:06:46.538 --> 00:06:49.808
All right.

00:06:49.808 --> 00:06:52.645
All right.
J.J., here we go.

00:06:52.645 --> 00:06:53.880
You already have two matches,

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:55.280
so you already
kind of have the win,

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:56.449
but this is the last one.

00:06:56.449 --> 00:06:58.050
All right?
All the money's on this one.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:01.053
I asked your brothers,
since you're the oldest sibling,

00:07:01.053 --> 00:07:05.357
what was your biggest
babysitting fail?

00:07:05.357 --> 00:07:08.027
-Oh, that's a loaded question.

00:07:08.027 --> 00:07:10.696
I mean, that -- that
has to be the chicken story.

00:07:10.696 --> 00:07:14.400
[ Laughter ]

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:17.103
-That is the story,
the chicken story.

00:07:17.103 --> 00:07:20.206
Watt brothers,
you guys are fantastic, man.

00:07:20.206 --> 00:07:22.741
I can't wait
to see you in person

00:07:22.741 --> 00:07:24.477
and see you on the field there.

00:07:24.477 --> 00:07:27.946
Have a great season, you guys.
And I really -- Stay safe, okay?

00:07:27.946 --> 00:07:29.849
And thank you for doing this.
It means a lot to me.

00:07:29.849 --> 00:07:31.283
-Thank you, Jimmy.
We appreciate it.

00:07:31.283 --> 00:07:32.618
-Bye, guys.
-Everybody stay safe.

00:07:32.618 --> 00:07:34.220
-Thanks, guys. Thanks so much.

